.SH NAME
ssoossh-host-mapping - Manage the local principal mapping file.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh host mapping [command] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manages the local principal mapping: a YAML file listing, per local account, the certificate principals allowed to assume it. Used by \fBhost principals\fR to answer sshd's AuthorizedPrincipalsCommand, and readable by pam_ssoossh's principals-map, so one file can serve both.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for mapping


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to the ssoossh config file

.PP
\fB--file\fP="/etc/ssoossh/principals.yaml"
	path to the local principal mapping file (YAML: local account -> list of principals)

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address including scheme (e.g. "https://example.com") assumes https if omited.

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


